_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/122279781?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/afalhambra-hivemq","html_url":"https://github.com/afalhambra-hivemq","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/afalhambra-hivemq/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/afalhambra-hivemq/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/afalhambra-hivemq/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/afalhambra-hivemq/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/afalhambra-hivemq/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/afalhambra-hivemq/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/afalhambra-hivemq/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/afalhambra-hivemq/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/afalhambra-hivemq/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-05-13T07:16:16Z","updated_at":"2026-05-13T07:16:16Z","body":"> I would not mind skipping retries on these status codes by default.\n\nuh, that would be even nicer! Although I still see this as a valid option to have as well","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lycheeverse/lychee/issues/comments/4438330836/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lycheeverse/lychee/issues/comments/4939349025","html_url":"https://github.com/lycheeverse/lychee/issues/2193#issuecomment-4939349025","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lycheeverse/lychee/issues/2193","id":4939349025,"node_id":"IC_kwDOEP6EKM8AAAABJmh8IQ","user":{"login":"costajohnt","id":14304404,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0MzA0NDA0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/14304404?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/costajohnt","html_url":"https://github.com/costajohnt","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/costajohnt/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/costajohnt/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/costajohnt/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/costajohnt/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/costajohnt/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/costajohnt/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/costajohnt/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/costajohnt/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/costajohnt/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-07-10T20:37:23Z","updated_at":"2026-07-10T20:37:23Z","body":"I started implementing this (subtractive `retry_skip_status_codes` config + CLI flag) and hit something worth checking before I open a PR.\n\nlychee doesn't actually retry 5xx status-code responses in the normal request path today, so subtracting 521/523/525/530 from the retry set would be a no-op for the exact case in the proposal. Quick empirical check with a mock server and `max_retries = 3`:\n\n- 500 -> 1 request\n- 521 -> 1 request\n- 523 -> 1 request\n- 429 -> 4 requests (1 + 3 retries)\n\nThe reason is that a 5xx response comes back as `Status::Error(ErrorKind::RejectedStatusCode(code))`, and `ErrorKind::should_retry` only returns true for 429 there. The `is_server_error()` branch in `RetryExt for StatusCode` only runs for `reqwest::Error` cases (transport-level), not for status-code responses. So `should_retry()` is already false for 521/523/525/530 and the retry loop returns before any skip list is consulted.\n\nOne nuance: real-world Cloudflare 52x that manifest as a connection timeout do get retried (`Status::Timeout`), but those carry no HTTP status code, so a numeric skip list can't target them either.\n\nSo before I build this out, which direction do you want?\n\n1. Make 5xx retryable first, then the subtractive skip makes sense (bigger change to the retry classification).\n2. If the retries you were seeing are the transport-level timeout case, that needs a different (non-numeric) knob.\n3. Scope the option to 429 only, since that's the one code it can actually govern today.\n\nHappy to implement whichever you prefer. I have the plumbing for a `StatusCodeSelector`-based option ready either way.\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lycheeverse/lychee/issues/comments/4939349025/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]